Mark 3ginfo.sh executable - LOCAL ONLY, not for upstream.

LuCI runs /usr/share/3ginfo-lite/3ginfo.sh directly via fs.exec, but upstream
ships the script non-executable (0644) and only chmods it in a first-boot
uci-defaults - so a fresh boot can fail before that uci-defaults runs. Upstream
declined-risk: they intentionally defer the chmod to first boot, so this stays
a local patch (split from 0001 so the logic change can be upstreamed alone).

Applies to: https://github.com/4IceG/luci-app-3ginfo-lite
            @ cbc144e527b067750f8986a033e2e00677d85fdf (pinned in feeds.conf.default)
Applied by: tools/cw-apply-feed-patches.sh after 0001 (sorted order).
Upstream status: not submitted (intentional local patch).

diff --git a/luci-app-3ginfo-lite/root/usr/share/3ginfo-lite/3ginfo.sh b/luci-app-3ginfo-lite/root/usr/share/3ginfo-lite/3ginfo.sh
old mode 100644
new mode 100755
